  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nA few high clouds will exit the area early this morning. After a \nchilly start in the mid-20s to lower 30s it will warm up nicely into \nthe upper 50s to low 60s with plenty of sunshine this afternoon. It \nwill be another cold one tonight with high pressure overhead. Sunday \nfeatures more sunshine and warm afternoon temperatures in the 60s. \nOur area remains under high pressure into Monday, with west winds \nincreasing between 5 to 10 mph. This setup will allow for additional \nwarming, with highs likely to reach well into the 60s and even near \n70 for the deeper valleys Monday afternoon. Skies will be sunny, \nexcept for a few late day clouds moving in from the north. \n\nA weak, moisture starved cold front will drop south through our area \nMonday night into Tuesday; providing a glancing blow of cooler air. \nSurface winds shift out of the north. Monday night features lows in \nthe upper 20s to 30s. Tuesday will see more sunny and dry \nconditions, but much cooler highs only in the upper 40s to 50s \nareawide. Canadian high pressure settles overhead Tuesday night, \nbringing light winds, clear skies and cold lows well down into the \n20s and low 30s. \n\nDry and mostly sunny weather continues for Wednesday, with a slow \nmoderating trend. South winds increase on Thursday out ahead of \nanother weak frontal boundary. Expected a few clouds around, but \nwarmer temperatures well into the 60s are in the forecast. Overall, \nother than a few slight chances for brief light rain, it now looks \nto remain dry and mild right through Halloween.",
